**About the Cause of Death Assistant project (CODA):**

The Cause of Death Assistant (CODA) is a three-year initiative to design and test an AI-powered tool for cause of death assignment in low- and middle-income countries (LMICs). CODA will address critical data gaps by improving the accuracy and timeliness of mortality data at both facility and community levels. The initiative is implemented by a consortium of global partners, with Vital Strategies serving as a CODA Consortium and Research Agenda Lead. Other consortium partners include an Algorithm Development Lead, an IT and Software Development Lead, and two Leads working on improved Minimally Invasive Tissue Sampling (MITS) protocols. Governance will be provided by a Governing Board and technical rigor overseen by a Scientific Advisory Committee (SAC). The SAC will convene Technical Working Groups (TWGs) to respond to specific technical demands encountered in the development of CODA and will be heavily involved in building research agendas. The project will be implemented in two phases: 1. Prototyping and 2. Experimentation (with phase 3 on piloting and product release to be undertaken as part of an anticipated follow-on grant). It is anticipated that by the end of the project, CODA will be positioned for adoption by countries, supported by regional Centers of Excellence (COEs) in Africa and South Asia.

**Job Purpose:**

The Principal Technical Advisor, Research, CODA, will lead and coordinate all research activities under the CODA project. This includes setting and managing the research agenda, ensuring technical and methodological rigor across all phases, producing high-quality knowledge products, and adhering to timelines. The Principal Technical Advisor, Research, CODA, will report to the Project Director, Consortium Lead, CODA, and will work closely with consortium partners, Centers of Excellence, the Scientific Advisory Committee, and Technical Working Groups to ensure that CODA research meets international standards, informs product development, and accelerates adoption at scale.

**Duties and Responsibilities:**

Working closely with the Project Director, Consortium Lead, CODA, and other consortium partners, the Principal Technical Advisor, Research will have the following specific responsibilities:

*Consortium Engagement & Representation -*

- Engage with the Scientific Advisory Committee and TWGs, ensuring that these bodies are updated on research progress and findings and that their technical advice informs project implementation;
- Work closely with consortium partners, Centers of Excellence, and experiment country stakeholders on issues related to research.

*Research & Technical Leadership -*

- Supported by the Senior Project Manager, lead the development of the overall CODA research agenda, aligned with project goals, user needs, and donor priorities;
- Lead the site selection process for experimentation phases of the project;
- Coordinate direct-funded research at experiment project sites, supporting study teams to ensure the timeliness of implementation and the quality, comparability, and relevance of research outputs;
- Lead the development of study protocols for the experimentation phase, including design, sampling, and analysis plans, ensuring COE and SAC input and Institutional Review Board (IRB) approval;
- Monitor the progress of each consortium partner's research agenda development and metrics gathering;
- Provide technical insights and contribute to the strengthening of the AI models and algorithms for cause-of-death assignment;
- Manage the project budget for experimental research;
- Provide project implementation support as needed by the Project Director;
- Contribute to progress monitoring and reporting on the project’s research and knowledge management activities.

*Ethics & Data Governance -*

- Lead the development of ethical guidelines and standards for CODA research;
- Contribute to the development of data governance and sharing agreements;
- Ensure adherence to ethical standards, IRB processes, and national regulations;
- Oversee data governance, privacy, and security protocols, including development of informed consent statements.

*Knowledge Generation & Management -*

- Supported by the Senior Project Manager, promote feedback loops to ensure research findings directly inform iterative product development;
- Lead knowledge management efforts, including global stakeholder engagement and journal supplements;
- Develop communication materials that summarize and convey the strength of the research agenda and summarize results for public scrutiny;
